course: dictionary
lesson: 14594
title: Plugged
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Plugged is the past form of the verb plug, so it can describe something that was connected, blocked or advertised.
explain: «The kettle was plugged in, so we made a cup of tea.» Here plugged in means connected to an electricity socket so it could work. The clues are kettle and tea, which both need electricity.
explain: «The sink was plugged with a rag, so the water could not drain.» Here plugged means blocked or filled, so nothing could pass through. Try your meaning in the sentence: blocked fits, and it still makes sense.
explain: Plugged can also mean a hole was filled to stop a leak, or that a book was advertised on TV. Always ask what fits the sentence, and look for helpful phrases like plugged in, plugged up and plugged the hole.
fact: Plug is a verb, so plugged is its past form: «I plugged in the lamp.»
fact: «Plugged in» means connected to an electricity socket so it can work.
fact: «Plugged up» means blocked, like a plugged drain or a stuffy nose.
fact: «Plugged» can also mean a hole was filled to stop a leak.
fact: Safety rule: never touch plugs or sockets with wet hands, and unplug things before you clean them.
exercise: «The fridge was plugged in all night.» What does plugged in mean? | Hidden under the table | Talked about on TV | *Connected to a socket so it can work | Blocked so nothing can pass
exercise: «My nose was plugged up, so I could not smell the toast.» What does plugged up mean? | Filled with paint to make it bright | *Blocked, so air cannot get through | Connected to electricity | Very tired and sleepy
exercise: «The leak was plugged with tape.» Find and copy the word that is a past form of plug. | with | *plugged | leak | tape
test: «Never touch a plug with wet hands.» What is the safety rule here? | Only use plugs in the bath | Touch plugs quickly with wet hands | Pull hard on the wire to remove it | *Keep your hands dry when you touch plugs
test: «The advert plugged the new film all week on TV.» What does plugged mean here? | Connected to electricity | Filled with water to stop a leak | *Talked about to advertise it | Blocked with dust
exam: Mia says, «The drain is plugged.» Which meaning fits best? | Plugged in and switched on | Very happy to be home | *Blocked, so water cannot get through | Talked about on TV
